# Build-context ALLOWLIST (S144): exclude everything, then let back in only the Dockerfile's COPY
# sources. On marvin the build context is the tenant root, a live checkout that also holds
# weewx-data/ (the archive, and conf backups with credentials), influxdb/ and logs/, and a plain
# `docker build` would hand all of it to the daemon. Adding a COPY source to the Dockerfile means
# adding it here too: tests/test_dockerignore.py fails until you do, and so does the build.
*
!Dockerfile
!patch
!requirements.txt
!logging.additions
!dewpoint_service.py
!pressure_service.py
!owm.py
!windy.py
!wcloud.py
!influx.py
!rtldavis.py
!entrypoint.sh
